<style>
  .letter-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(21px, 2.1vw, 25px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 13px;
  }
  .letter-block {
    max-width: 660px;
  }
  .letter-block .letter-body {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .kit-sub {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .letter-body {
    margin-top: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 17px;
  }
  .letter-body p {
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>

{% comment %} <section class="sec-cream" id="skeptical" data-screen-label="Skeptical">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="letter-block reveal in">
      <h2 class="dl">Let me guess what you are thinking.</h2>
      <div class="letter-body">
        <p>You have probably seen the cheap ones. And you are wondering if this is the same plastic in a nicer box.</p>
        <p>You are right to be skeptical. I would be.</p>
        <p>
          Here is the difference, plainly. A stock tray is one shape, cut once, shipped to everybody. It cannot look
          like it belongs to your face, because it was never made for your face. Your set starts with impressions of
          your own teeth, and it does not ship until it passes all seven checkpoints against those impressions.
        </p>
        <p>Not a mold that approximates your mouth. Your mouth, your teeth, your bite.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section> {% endcomment %}
<section class="sec-cream" id="skeptical" data-screen-label="{{ section.settings.screen_label }}">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="letter-block reveal in">
      <h2 class="dl">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>

      <div class="letter-body">
        {{ section.settings.content }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


{% schema %}
    {
      "name": "Guess Section",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "screen_label",
          "label": "Screen Label",
          "default": "Skeptical"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Let me guess what you are thinking."
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "content",
          "label": "Content",
          "default": "<p>You have probably seen the cheap ones. And you are wondering if this is the same plastic in a nicer box.</p><p>You are right to be skeptical. I would be.</p><p>Here is the difference, plainly. A stock tray is one shape, cut once, shipped to everybody. It cannot look like it belongs to your face, because it was never made for your face. Your set starts with impressions of your own teeth, and it does not ship until it passes all seven checkpoints against those impressions.</p><p>Not a mold that approximates your mouth. Your mouth, your teeth, your bite.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "presets": [
        {
          "name": "Guess Section"
        }
      ]
    }
    {% endschema %}